component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a new histology-to-spatial-transcriptomics prediction model. The model uses H&E slides and pathology foundation model tokens, but no natural-language text component is described.","evidence_snippet":"predicting spatially resolved gene expression directly from the haematoxylin and eosin (H&E) slides; foundation-model tokens"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000093","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary multimodal prediction model that explicitly integrates pathology reports with histopathology images and transcriptomic features. The text-bio linkage is central to the pretrained multimodal foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"pretrained on paired histopathology images, RNA sequencing, and pathology reports; integrating clinicopathologic variables, transcriptomic features, and multiscale histopathology-derived image representations"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000094","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This manuscript is explicitly a narrative review of AI-based mpMRI approaches for biochemical recurrence prediction. It summarizes existing studies rather than introducing a new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"This manuscript is a narrative review; no systematic protocol was registered"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000095","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of generalist foundation models and quantum computing in oncology, not a primary model paper. The abstract does not describe a substantive text-bio generative model.","evidence_snippet":"This review fills in these gaps ... this review aims to critically discuss the potential of quantum computing (QC) to augment GMAI"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000096","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary cancer classification model built on gene expression profiling. Gene-expression tokenization and spiking-transformer modeling do not provide a natural-language text component or text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"model SpikeFormer ... to model complex temporal dependencies in gene expression data; evaluated on The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) dataset"}]}
